       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. A single 1600 mg dose is also above the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. The risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events goes up a lot at that dose, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum dose)\n- **800 mg by mouth, 3 times daily** (2,400 mg/day, a common anti-inflammatory regimen)\n- **400 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **1600 mg/day** divided in some other way\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and include a note with the rationale. I'd still suggest confirming it with pharmacy. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
