       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical rationale for 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen. That's double the maximum daily dose. I don't know of any indication that would justify it, and it could seriously harm the patient through GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, or cardiovascular events.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- Enter a dose within the labeled maximum, such as 800 mg by mouth 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day) or 800 mg 3 times daily.\n- Enter a different regimen if the goal is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect. Options include scheduled acetaminophen alongside ibuprofen, or another agent. Pharmacy can help choose.\n- If you have a specific clinical reason for exceeding the maximum, discuss it with pharmacy and enter it through the pharmacy override process. I can't make that decision for you, and I'd want that review on record.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it now."
